Licence of the O'Hara-Rudy (ORd) parts of cipaord_endo.mmt
==========================================================

cipaord_endo.mmt is a Myokit re-expression of the CiPAORdv1.0 model. Its ORd core
(CaMKII, reversal potentials, INa, INaL, Ito, ICaL/ICaNa/ICaK, IKs, IK1, INaCa, INaK,
background currents and IpCa, SR release and uptake, diffusion/translocation fluxes,
buffering and concentrations, and cell geometry) follows the O'Hara-Rudy reference
implementation as distributed in the FDA CiPA repository
(https://github.com/FDA/CiPA, AP_simulation/models/newordherg_qNet.c, commit 539ff80,
cloned 2026-11-01). Those parts are derived from code under the BSD 3-clause licence
below; its copyright notice, conditions and disclaimer are reproduced exactly as they
appear in the header of that C file (with the C comment markers "// " removed).

The rest of cipaord_endo.mmt (the hERG Markov model with drug binding and trapping,
written in flux form from Li et al. 2017; the virtual-drug scaling of Parikh et al.
2019; the qNet integral; the stimulus and protocol) and the other code of this data set
are new and licensed MIT, as is the repository. No code of the FDA's own (GPL-3.0)
contributions to that C file is included.

